    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds okay but i'm a bit worried about getting too tired or hitting a wall midway through. like how do i know if i'm pushing too hard or if the fatigue is just normal? can u give me a bit more detail on how to handle those days where i feel really drained?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Listen closely to your body; fatigue that feels like sharp pain is too much, but general soreness is normal. If you feel completely drained on a scheduled heavy day, it's better to reduce the weight by 10-15% than to risk injury. On those days, cut back to just one working set of your main lifts, focusing solely on perfect form. Prioritize recovery by ensuring you are getting good sleep and proper nutrition when training feels overwhelming.",
      "source": "target",
